@startuml
' Figure 6.8 – State diagram: the article lifecycle
' Placement and visibility are not free-form: the transitions below are the only
' ones the API permits, and one of them is deliberately one-way.
!include ../_style.puml
hide empty description

[*] --> Draft : create

state Draft {
  Draft : content saved automatically
  Draft : invisible to everyone but the author
}

state "Published — public, free" as PubFree {
  PubFree : in the public feed
  PubFree : body readable by guests
}

state "Published — public, premium" as PubPremium {
  PubPremium : in the public feed
  PubPremium : body requires a premium plan
}

state "Listed — marketplace" as Market {
  Market : absent from the public feed
  Market : priced in credits
  Market : body requires a preview or a purchase
}

state "Owned by a magazine" as Owned {
  Owned : one full purchase, exclusive
  Owned : still on the marketplace, not public
  Owned : in the magazine's library, waiting
}

state "Published by a magazine" as PubMag {
  PubMag : public and free, price cleared
  PubMag : publisherId names the magazine
  PubMag : publishedAt left untouched
}

state Deleted {
  Deleted : deleted_at is set
  Deleted : chunks removed by an explicit job
}

Draft --> PubFree : publish\n[placement = public, visibility = free]
Draft --> PubPremium : publish\n[placement = public, visibility = premium]\n[writer is eligible]
Draft --> Market : publish\n[placement = marketplace, price > 0]\n[writer is eligible]

PubFree --> PubFree : update\n/ re-embed, refresh the voice profile
PubPremium --> PubPremium : update
Market --> Market : update

Market --> PubFree : abandon the sale\n[one-way, no full purchase]
Market --> PubPremium : abandon the sale\n[one-way, no full purchase]
Market --> Owned : full purchase by a magazine\n[no other magazine owns it]
Owned --> PubMag : the magazine publishes\n/ public, free, publisher recorded

PubFree --> Deleted : soft delete
PubPremium --> Deleted : soft delete
Market --> Deleted : soft delete\n[no full purchase]
Draft --> Deleted : soft delete
Deleted --> [*]

note right of Market
  public → marketplace is refused by the API. An article
  the public has already read has no exclusivity left to
  sell, so the switch runs one way only.
end note

note right of Owned
  Once a magazine owns the article, the writer can
  neither switch it to public nor delete it, and no
  other magazine can preview or buy it: each is
  refused with 409 (FR-72).
end note

note bottom of Deleted
  A soft delete does not cascade: the row survives, so
  ON DELETE CASCADE never fires. The chunks are removed
  by a remove-article-chunks job, or a deleted article's
  text stays retrievable into prompts.
end note
@enduml
